WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: LOGIC-ONLY — cursor_meta.rs defined the
unified contract with a FakeTerminal unit test and zero production
callers)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- DeltaJournal carries the per-surface cursor registry
  (serde-defaulted `surfaces`: pre-M4.5 journals deserialize unchanged).
- shell.run records a TERMINAL CursorMeta through the exact unified
  contract (surface=Terminal, handle=broker run id, position=output
  byte length, live=false after exit) and persists it in an
  epoch-fenced WorktreeCheckpointed event. Reattachment resumes output
  from the captured position via the broker's offset-addressed reads
  (Phase 2.6 machinery).
- Browser/Sandbox ride the SAME contract as typed SurfaceKinds; their
  producers arrive with M7/M8. The interface and the durable capture
  path are proven once, on the terminal surface, today — no placeholder
  browser/sandbox producers were invented.

